{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>For her wounds are incurable (אנושה)</b>: each one of her blows. And like it: <i>incurable is your fracture (אנוש לשברך)</i> — from the same root as <i>and he became dangerously ill (ויאנש)</i>." "<b>Incurable (אנושה)</b>: it is an adjective, like <i>mighty (עצומה)</i>, <i>blessed (ברוכה)</i>. For the blow reached Judah, for Sennacherib captured the fortified cities of Judah."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:35.323468410Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}